From fe09dd005a8272e22f3cb817b4d010a382884d0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:06:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add a "Groups in common" tab to the personal chat info

Reads the server's existing GET /common-groups/<wid> route (wa-js
WPP.contact.getCommonGroups) and lists the groups the user shares with
the contact. Client-only: nothing in WPPConnect or client/api_patches
changes.

wa-js answers [] both for "no groups in common" and for "contact not
loaded in the page", so an empty answer also asks the other JID form of
the person (phone <-> @lid) before settling on "none", and a failed
request is told apart from an empty one ("unavailable" vs "none").
The reply is the bare Wid array, read as strings or objects, envelope
tolerated. Names come from the local chat list, never a raw JID.

The tab is last, so Overview and Media keep their positions. Enter or
Space on a group opens that conversation. Logic is in core/common_groups.py
and the tab in a mixin, keeping the 2000-line dialog from growing.
The existing tab-order test now expects the third tab.
